#!/bin/bash

# omarchy:summary=Install or reconcile the Omarchy desktop overlay in stages
# omarchy:args=[packages|artifacts|register] <stage>... [--check] [--repair] [--theme <name>] [--all-configs] [--no-session-entry]
# omarchy:examples=omarchy overlay setup core | omarchy overlay setup link config | omarchy overlay setup packages core audio | omarchy overlay setup all
# omarchy:requires-sudo=true

set -euo pipefail

usage() {
  cat <<'USAGE'
Usage: omarchy-overlay-setup [packages|artifacts|register] <stage>... [--check] [--repair] [--theme <name>] [--all-configs] [--no-session-entry]

Sets up the Omarchy desktop (Hyprland + Quickshell + themes) from this source
checkout on an Arch system that Omarchy did not install, one stage at a time.
It refuses to run where the omarchy product packages are installed. The host
keeps ownership of boot, storage, disk security, and networking:

  - configures nothing in the host's boot, storage, or disk-security stack:
    bootloader, initramfs generation, Secure Boot, disk encryption,
    partitioning, and Snapper are left exactly as they are
  - installs no display manager unless the display-manager stage is named
    explicitly; that stage is excluded from "all" and records a rollback
  - never installs the omarchy or omarchy-settings packages
  - never enables system services except sddm.service in the explicit
    display-manager stage

Setup stages print their package and file changes before acting and are
idempotent. The rollback stage consumes its active transaction when complete:

  core           Compositor, uwsm, Quickshell, portals, foot, fonts, and the
                 runtime tools Omarchy's desktop scripts invoke. Adds the
                 [omarchy] pacman repo if absent (timestamped .bak kept), pins
                 its signing key, and installs omarchy-keyring. The pinned key
                 is added to /etc/pacman.d/gnupg when absent.
  link           Point the system at this checkout: /etc/omarchy.conf via
                 the shared runtime-link writer without a sudo path, plus
                 ~/.config/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy (existing file backed up to
                 ~/.config/uwsm/backups/). The development sudoers policy
                 that puts the checkout on root's secure_path is deliberately
                 NOT installed: omarchy commands escalate internally, and a
                 user-writable bin/ on secure_path is a development trust
                 grant, not a production one. Developers who want
                 "sudo omarchy-*" resolution use a product development link;
                 dev link and unlink are refused after overlay registration.
  config         Seed desktop configs into ~/.config (backups kept), install
                 the icon font and default branding (existing branding is
                 preserved), generate the initial theme, and mark
                 package-dependent first-run provisioning complete.
                 Requires link.
  audio          PipeWire pulse/alsa bridges, WirePlumber, volume controls.
  files          File manager, previews, mounts, automount; registers the
                 default directory handler when xdg-mime is available.
  connectivity   Network and bluetooth daemons for the shell's panels
                 (installed only, never enabled).
  capture        Screenshots, recording, color picker, OCR, QR tools.
  power          Brightness and power-profile controls.
  lock           Lock-screen PAM services (/etc/pam.d/omarchy-lock-*) via
                 omarchy-apply-lock. Explicit opt-in.
  session-entry  Greeter session file under
                 /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/. Explicit opt-in.
  display-manager
                 Install and configure SDDM with Omarchy's Wayland greeter,
                 authenticated login, and session entry; enable it for the
                 next boot without starting it now. Explicit opt-in and never
                 included in "all". Refuses to replace another display
                 manager. Records the prior files, enabled state, and default
                 target before changing them. The minimal greeter logs in
                 SDDM's remembered last user and intentionally has no user
                 chooser, matching Omarchy's single-user workstation model.
  display-manager-rollback
                 Disable SDDM when this setup enabled it and restore the exact
                 files and default target recorded by display-manager. Leaves
                 installed packages in place to avoid removing dependencies
                 another host package may now use.
  status         Read-only report of what each stage has and hasn't done.
  all            Every desktop stage above in dependency order, through the
                 session entry, but never display-manager (the one-shot setup
                 for disposable machines and CI).

Package stages run one combined "pacman -Syu --needed" for everything
selected, so the host's own pacman hooks run exactly as a plain -Syu would —
a kernel update, for example, rebuilds the host's initramfs with the host's
configuration. Registering the overlay makes this same full system upgrade part
of `omarchy update`; Arch does not support partial system upgrades.

Dependency order: core -> link -> config. Display-manager needs all three;
every other setup stage only needs core. Rollback stands alone.

By default config seeds only the desktop's own configs (Hyprland, the Omarchy
shell, foot, and the other tools these stages install); --all-configs seeds
every shipped config (git, tmux, Chromium, ...) the way a packaged install
would.

Once registered, `omarchy update` selects the desktop-overlay update path. That
path fast-forwards the checkout, reconciles packages for the recorded stages,
runs desktop-overlay migrations, and never runs product migrations or touches
the host's boot, storage, or disk-security configuration.

Modes:
  packages             Reconcile packages for already-recorded package stages
                       without reapplying any stage files. Core reconciliation
                       restores an absent [omarchy] stanza and pinned key first.
  artifacts            Reconcile already-recorded static system artifacts for
                       lock, session-entry, or display-manager without a
                       package transaction. Display-manager artifacts preserve
                       SDDM's enabled state, default target, and runtime state.
  register             Record an existing, successfully probed overlay without
                       reapplying packages, configuration, or system files.
                       Add --repair to replace a stale or malformed descriptor
                       after the same probes succeed.

Options:
  --theme <name>      Initial theme for the config stage (default: tokyo-night)
  --all-configs       Seed every shipped config, not just the desktop's
  --no-session-entry  Drop the session-entry stage from "all"
  --check             Validate an artifacts operation without writing
  --repair            Replace an existing descriptor during registration, or
                      recover an invalid descriptor and missing core packages
                      with setup core --repair
  -h, --help          Show this help

To adopt an existing checkout-backed desktop, run this from its checkout:

  ./bin/omarchy-overlay-register core link config audio files connectivity capture power lock session-entry display-manager

Omit stages that are not installed, then add them later with
`omarchy overlay setup <stage>...`.
USAGE
}

# Overridable for tests only; real runs always target the /etc paths.
system_root="${OMARCHY_OVERLAY_SETUP_SYSTEM_ROOT:-${OMARCHY_DEV_SETUP_SYSTEM_ROOT:-}}"
system_path() {
  printf '%s%s' "$system_root" "$1"
}

pacman_conf="${OMARCHY_OVERLAY_SETUP_PACMAN_CONF:-${OMARCHY_DEV_SETUP_PACMAN_CONF:-$(system_path /etc/pacman.conf)}}"
omarchy_conf="${OMARCHY_OVERLAY_SETUP_OMARCHY_CONF:-${OMARCHY_DEV_SETUP_OMARCHY_CONF:-$(system_path /etc/omarchy.conf)}}"
installation_conf="${OMARCHY_INSTALLATION_CONF_PATH:-$(system_path /etc/omarchy/installation.conf)}"
omarchy_signing_key="40DFB630FF42BCFFB047046CF0134EE680CAC571"
current_user=$(id -un)

package_stages=(core audio files connectivity capture power display-manager)
all_stages=(core link config audio files connectivity capture power lock session-entry)
known_stages=(core link config audio files connectivity capture power lock session-entry display-manager)

# Only configuration the desktop these stages install actually reads.
# Everything else under config/ changes unrelated application behavior
# (git, tmux, Chromium, ...) and stays opt-in via --all-configs.
desktop_configs=(autostart btop foot hypr hyprland-preview-share-picker omarchy wireplumber)

theme="tokyo-night"
session_entry=1
all_configs=0
repair_registration=0
setup_core_repair=0
check_artifacts=0
operation=setup
declare -A selected=()
declare -A recorded=()
status_only=1

if [[ ${1:-} == "packages" || ${1:-} == "artifacts" || ${1:-} == "register" ]]; then
  operation="$1"
  shift
fi

while (($#)); do
  case "$1" in
    --theme)
      theme="${2:-}"
      if [[ -z $theme ]]; then
        echo "Error: --theme needs a theme name" >&2
        exit 1
      fi
      shift 2
      ;;
    --all-configs)
      all_configs=1
      shift
      ;;
    --no-session-entry)
      session_entry=0
      shift
      ;;
    --repair)
      repair_registration=1
      shift
      ;;
    --check)
      check_artifacts=1
      shift
      ;;
    -h|--help)
      usage
      exit 0
      ;;
    core|link|config|audio|files|connectivity|capture|power|lock|session-entry|display-manager|display-manager-rollback|status)
      selected[$1]=1
      shift
      ;;
    all)
      for stage in "${all_stages[@]}"; do
        selected[$stage]=1
      done
      shift
      ;;
    *)
      echo "Unknown stage or option: $1" >&2
      usage >&2
      exit 1
      ;;
  esac
done

if (( ${#selected[@]} == 0 )); then
  usage >&2
  exit 1
fi

if (( session_entry == 0 )); then
  if [[ -n ${selected[display-manager]:-} ]]; then
    echo "Error: display-manager requires its Omarchy session entry; remove --no-session-entry." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  unset 'selected[session-entry]'
  if (( ${#selected[@]} == 0 )); then
    echo "Error: --no-session-entry removed the only selected stage; nothing to do." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

if [[ -n ${selected[display-manager]:-} && $operation != "packages" ]]; then
  selected[session-entry]=1
fi

if [[ -n ${selected[display-manager-rollback]:-} ]] && (( ${#selected[@]} != 1 )); then
  echo "Error: display-manager-rollback must be run by itself." >&2
  exit 1
fi
if [[ -n ${selected[status]:-} ]] && (( ${#selected[@]} != 1 )); then
  echo "Error: status must be run by itself." >&2
  exit 1
fi

if [[ $operation != "setup" ]]; then
  if [[ -n ${selected[status]:-} || -n ${selected[display-manager-rollback]:-} ]]; then
    echo "Error: $operation accepts setup stages only." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if [[ $operation == "packages" ]]; then
    for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
      is_package_stage=0
      for package_stage in "${package_stages[@]}"; do
        if [[ $stage == "$package_stage" ]]; then
          is_package_stage=1
          break
        fi
      done
      if (( ! is_package_stage )); then
        echo "Error: packages cannot reconcile non-package stage '$stage'." >&2
        exit 1
      fi
    done
  elif [[ $operation == "artifacts" ]]; then
    for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
      if [[ $stage != "lock" && $stage != "session-entry" && $stage != "display-manager" ]]; then
        echo "Error: artifacts cannot reconcile stage '$stage'." >&2
        exit 1
      fi
    done
  fi
  if [[ $theme != "tokyo-night" ]] || (( all_configs || ! session_entry )); then
    echo "Error: --theme, --all-configs, and --no-session-entry are setup-only options." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

if (( repair_registration )); then
  if [[ $operation == "register" ]]; then
    :
  elif [[ $operation == "setup" && -n ${selected[core]:-} ]] && (( ${#selected[@]} == 1 )); then
    setup_core_repair=1
  else
    echo "Error: --repair is valid with register, or with setup core by itself." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi
if (( check_artifacts )) && [[ $operation != "artifacts" ]]; then
  echo "Error: --check is valid only with artifacts." >&2
  exit 1
fi

for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
  if [[ $stage != "status" ]]; then
    status_only=0
  fi
done

if (( EUID == 0 )); then
  echo "Error: run omarchy-overlay-setup as your user, not under sudo." >&2
  exit 1
fi

checkout=$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "$(realpath "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")")/.." && pwd)
manifest="$checkout/install/omarchy-desktop.packages"
export OMARCHY_PATH="$checkout"
export PATH="$checkout/bin:$PATH"
# shellcheck source=../install/helpers/runtime-link.sh
source "$checkout/install/helpers/runtime-link.sh"

if [[ ! -f $manifest ]]; then
  echo "Error: $manifest not found — is this an Omarchy source checkout?" >&2
  exit 1
fi

group_packages() {
  awk -v group="$1" '
    /^# group: / { in_group = ($3 == group); next }
    { sub(/[[:space:]]*#.*$/, "") }
    in_group && NF { print }
  ' "$manifest"
}

ensure_overlay_package_source() {
  if ! grep -q '^\[omarchy\]' "$pacman_conf"; then
    echo "    writes: [omarchy] repo stanza in $pacman_conf (backup kept)"
    sudo cp -f "$pacman_conf" "$pacman_conf.omarchy-overlay-setup.$(date +%s).bak"
    # Omarchy packages carry detached signatures, while the repository database
    # is currently unsigned. Require package signatures without requiring a
    # database signature that the repository does not publish.
    # shellcheck disable=SC2016
    printf '\n[omarchy]\nSigLevel = Required DatabaseOptional\nServer = https://pkgs.omarchy.org/stable/$arch\n' | sudo tee -a "$pacman_conf" >/dev/null
  fi

  echo "    verifies: Omarchy package signing key $omarchy_signing_key"
  if ! sudo pacman-key --list-keys "$omarchy_signing_key" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "    writes: pinned Omarchy package signing key in /etc/pacman.d/gnupg"
    sudo pacman-key --recv-keys "$omarchy_signing_key" --keyserver keys.openpgp.org
  fi
  sudo pacman-key --lsign-key "$omarchy_signing_key"
}

stage_selected() {
  [[ -n ${selected[$1]:-} ]]
}

# Compatibility path: existing desktop installations keep their original
# rollback here. Renaming the command must never orphan those transactions.
display_manager_state_root="$HOME/.local/state/omarchy/dev-setup-desktop/display-manager"
display_manager_active_file="$display_manager_state_root/active"
# Frozen index mapping for transactions created before the versioned inventory.
# Never reorder or extend this array; change display_manager_paths instead.
display_manager_legacy_paths=(
  "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-theme.conf)"
  "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-wayland.conf)"
  "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/99-omarchy-login.conf)"
  "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/autologin.conf)"
  "$(system_path /usr/share/sddm/hyprland.lua)"
  "$(system_path /usr/share/sddm/themes/omarchy)"
  "$(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop)"
  "$(system_path /var/lib/sddm/state.conf)"
)
display_manager_paths=("${display_manager_legacy_paths[@]}")
display_manager_recorded_paths=()

validate_display_manager_paths() {
  local path relative
  local -A seen=()

  (( $# > 0 )) || return 1
  for path in "$@"; do
    # An inventory is data, never shell code or an arbitrary sudo destination.
    # This scope also permits restoring retired SDDM config files.
    [[ $path == "$system_root"/* ]] || return 1
    relative=${path#"$system_root"}
    case "$relative" in
      /usr/share/sddm/hyprland.lua|/usr/share/sddm/themes/omarchy|/usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop|/var/lib/sddm/state.conf) ;;
      *) [[ $relative =~ ^/etc/sddm\.conf\.d/[a-zA-Z0-9_-][a-zA-Z0-9_.-]*\.conf$ ]] || return 1 ;;
    esac
    [[ -z ${seen[$path]:-} ]] || return 1
    seen[$path]=1
  done
}

read_display_manager_inventory() {
  local transaction_dir="$1" version

  display_manager_recorded_paths=()
  if [[ -e $transaction_dir/inventory || -L $transaction_dir/inventory ]]; then
    [[ -f $transaction_dir/inventory && ! -L $transaction_dir/inventory ]] || return 1
    {
      IFS= read -r version || return 1
      [[ $version == "1" ]] || return 1
      mapfile -t display_manager_recorded_paths
    } <"$transaction_dir/inventory"
  else
    display_manager_recorded_paths=("${display_manager_legacy_paths[@]}")
  fi
  validate_display_manager_paths "${display_manager_recorded_paths[@]}"
}

write_display_manager_inventory() {
  local transaction_dir="$1"

  if ! validate_display_manager_paths "${display_manager_recorded_paths[@]}"; then
    echo "Error: refusing to write an invalid display-manager path inventory; existing transaction is unchanged." >&2
    return 1
  fi
  printf '%s\n' 1 "${display_manager_recorded_paths[@]}" >"$transaction_dir/inventory.new"
  mv -- "$transaction_dir/inventory.new" "$transaction_dir/inventory"
}

capture_display_manager_path() {
  local transaction_dir="$1" index="$2" path="$3"

  if sudo test -e "$path" || sudo test -L "$path"; then
    # A retry after interruption must replace the incomplete unpublished copy.
    sudo rm -rf -- "$transaction_dir/backup/$index"
    sudo cp -aT "$path" "$transaction_dir/backup/$index"
    printf 'present\n' >"$transaction_dir/path-$index-state"
    echo "    rollback: captured $path"
  else
    printf 'absent\n' >"$transaction_dir/path-$index-state"
    echo "    rollback: recorded absent path $path"
  fi
}

config_stage_complete() {
  [[ -f $HOME/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua &&
    -f $HOME/.config/omarchy/branding/about.txt &&
    -f $HOME/.config/omarchy/branding/screensaver.txt &&
    -f $HOME/.local/state/omarchy/done/first-run-user &&
    -L $HOME/.config/btop/themes/current.theme ]]
}

display_manager_transaction_id() {
  local transaction_id

  [[ -f $display_manager_active_file ]] || return 1
  IFS= read -r transaction_id <"$display_manager_active_file"
  [[ $transaction_id =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || return 1
  [[ -d $display_manager_state_root/transactions/$transaction_id ]] || return 1
  printf '%s' "$transaction_id"
}

validate_display_manager_transaction() {
  local transaction_id="$1"
  local transaction_dir="$display_manager_state_root/transactions/$transaction_id"
  local index state

  [[ -f $transaction_dir/sddm-enabled-before ]] || return 1
  state=$(<"$transaction_dir/sddm-enabled-before")
  [[ $state == "enabled" || $state == "disabled" ]] || return 1

  [[ -f $transaction_dir/default-target-before ]] || return 1
  state=$(<"$transaction_dir/default-target-before")
  [[ $state == "graphical.target" || $state == "multi-user.target" ]] || return 1

  read_display_manager_inventory "$transaction_dir" || return 1
  for index in "${!display_manager_recorded_paths[@]}"; do
    [[ -f $transaction_dir/path-$index-state ]] || return 1
    state=$(<"$transaction_dir/path-$index-state")
    if [[ $state == "present" ]]; then
      [[ -e $transaction_dir/backup/$index || -L $transaction_dir/backup/$index ]] || return 1
    elif [[ $state != "absent" ]]; then
      return 1
    fi
  done
}

display_manager_artifacts_installed() {
  local theme_source="$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy"
  local theme_target
  theme_target=$(system_path /usr/share/sddm/themes/omarchy)

  package_requirement_satisfied sddm || return 1
  package_requirement_satisfied qt6-wayland || return 1
  cmp -s "$checkout/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-theme.conf" "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-theme.conf)" || return 1
  cmp -s "$checkout/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-wayland.conf" "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-wayland.conf)" || return 1
  cmp -s "$checkout/default/sddm/hyprland.lua" "$(system_path /usr/share/sddm/hyprland.lua)" || return 1
  cmp -s "$checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" "$(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop)" || return 1
  diff -qr "$theme_source" "$theme_target" >/dev/null 2>&1 || return 1
  cmp -s <(printf '[Users]\nRememberLastUser=true\nRememberLastSession=true\n') \
    "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/99-omarchy-login.conf)" || return 1
}

display_manager_configured() {
  display_manager_artifacts_installed || return 1
  systemctl is-enabled --quiet sddm.service 2>/dev/null || return 1
  [[ $(systemctl get-default 2>/dev/null) == "graphical.target" ]]
}

preflight_display_manager() {
  local source alias_path alias_target default_target transaction_id

  if ! validate_display_manager_paths "${display_manager_paths[@]}"; then
    echo "Error: the managed display-manager paths are outside the supported scope, empty, or duplicated; fix the checkout before applying this stage." >&2
    return 1
  fi

  for source in \
    "$checkout/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-theme.conf" \
    "$checkout/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-wayland.conf" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/hyprland.lua" \
    "$checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/Main.qml" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/metadata.desktop" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/theme.conf" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/bullet.png" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/entry.png" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/entry-failed.png" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/lock.png" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/lock-failed.png" \
    "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy/logo.png"; do
    if [[ ! -f $source ]]; then
      echo "Error: required SDDM source is missing: $source" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  done
  if [[ ! -d $checkout/default/sddm/omarchy ]]; then
    echo "Error: required SDDM theme is missing: $checkout/default/sddm/omarchy" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if find "$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy" -type l -print -quit | grep -q .; then
    echo "Error: the SDDM theme contains a symlink; refusing to publish checkout-controlled links under /usr/share/sddm." >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  alias_path=$(system_path /etc/systemd/system/display-manager.service)
  if [[ -e $alias_path || -L $alias_path ]]; then
    alias_target=$(readlink -f "$alias_path" 2>/dev/null || true)
    if [[ $(basename "$alias_target") != "sddm.service" ]]; then
      if [[ $operation == "artifacts" ]]; then
        echo "Error: the recorded display-manager stage no longer owns $alias_path: ${alias_target:-unresolvable}" >&2
        display_manager_repair_guidance
      else
        echo "Error: another display manager owns $alias_path: ${alias_target:-unresolvable}" >&2
        echo "Disable it explicitly before selecting display-manager; this setup will not replace it." >&2
      fi
      exit 1
    fi
  fi

  if [[ $operation == "setup" ]]; then
    default_target=$(systemctl get-default 2>/dev/null || true)
    if [[ $default_target != "graphical.target" && $default_target != "multi-user.target" ]]; then
      echo "Error: unsupported default systemd target '$default_target'; expected graphical.target or multi-user.target." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  fi

  if [[ -f $display_manager_active_file ]]; then
    transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id || true)
    if [[ -z $transaction_id ]] || ! validate_display_manager_transaction "$transaction_id"; then
      echo "Error: the active display-manager rollback record is invalid: $display_manager_active_file" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  elif [[ $operation == "artifacts" ]]; then
    echo "Error: display-manager artifact reconciliation requires its original rollback transaction: $display_manager_active_file" >&2
    display_manager_repair_guidance
    echo "Refusing to replace it with a post-install baseline." >&2
    exit 1
  elif display_manager_artifacts_installed; then
    echo "Error: the Omarchy display manager is already configured, but its original rollback transaction is missing." >&2
    echo "Repair the registration with the currently installed stages while omitting display-manager." >&2
    echo "Refusing to record the installed Omarchy files as a false pre-install baseline." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
}

display_manager_repair_guidance() {
  local stage command="omarchy overlay register --repair"

  for stage in "${known_stages[@]}"; do
    if [[ $stage != "display-manager" && -n ${recorded[$stage]:-} ]]; then
      command+=" $stage"
    fi
  done
  echo "The current greeter and stored rollback files will remain unchanged." >&2
  echo "Stop managing the stale stage by repairing the ledger while omitting display-manager:" >&2
  echo "  $command" >&2
  echo "After repairing the host state, re-adopt it with 'omarchy overlay setup display-manager'." >&2
}

begin_display_manager_transaction() {
  local transaction_id transaction_dir index path recorded_path found

  transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id || true)
  if [[ -n $transaction_id ]]; then
    validate_display_manager_transaction "$transaction_id" || {
      echo "Error: refusing to reuse an invalid display-manager rollback record." >&2
      return 1
    }
    transaction_dir="$display_manager_state_root/transactions/$transaction_id"
    # Publish the legacy mapping before extending it. New paths are captured
    # before the inventory is atomically extended and before any artifact write.
    write_display_manager_inventory "$transaction_dir"
    for path in "${display_manager_paths[@]}"; do
      found=0
      for recorded_path in "${display_manager_recorded_paths[@]}"; do
        if [[ $path == "$recorded_path" ]]; then
          found=1
          break
        fi
      done
      if (( ! found )); then
        index=${#display_manager_recorded_paths[@]}
        capture_display_manager_path "$transaction_dir" "$index" "$path"
        display_manager_recorded_paths+=("$path")
        write_display_manager_inventory "$transaction_dir"
      fi
    done
    echo "    rollback: reusing transaction $transaction_id"
    return 0
  fi

  transaction_id=$(date +%s%N)
  transaction_dir="$display_manager_state_root/transactions/$transaction_id"
  mkdir -p "$transaction_dir/backup"
  chmod 0700 "$display_manager_state_root" "$display_manager_state_root/transactions" "$transaction_dir" "$transaction_dir/backup"

  if systemctl is-enabled --quiet sddm.service 2>/dev/null; then
    printf 'enabled\n' >"$transaction_dir/sddm-enabled-before"
  else
    printf 'disabled\n' >"$transaction_dir/sddm-enabled-before"
  fi
  systemctl get-default >"$transaction_dir/default-target-before"

  for index in "${!display_manager_paths[@]}"; do
    path="${display_manager_paths[$index]}"
    capture_display_manager_path "$transaction_dir" "$index" "$path"
  done
  display_manager_recorded_paths=("${display_manager_paths[@]}")
  write_display_manager_inventory "$transaction_dir"

  printf '%s\n' "$transaction_id" >"$display_manager_active_file.new"
  mv "$display_manager_active_file.new" "$display_manager_active_file"
  echo "    rollback: recorded transaction $transaction_id under $display_manager_state_root"
}

apply_display_manager() {
  local login_config state_config state_path theme_source theme_target theme_file relative_theme_file autologin_path preserved_dir transaction_id

  echo "    writes: /etc/sddm.conf.d/{10-theme,10-wayland,99-omarchy-login}.conf"
  echo "    writes: /usr/share/sddm/{hyprland.lua,themes/omarchy/}"
  echo "    writes: /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop"
  if [[ $operation == "setup" ]]; then
    echo "    seeds when absent: /var/lib/sddm/state.conf (last user/session only; no autologin)"
    echo "    enables: sddm.service for the next boot (not started now)"
  else
    echo "    preserves: SDDM enabled state, default target, runtime state.conf, and autologin.conf"
  fi

  sudo install -Dm644 "$checkout/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-theme.conf" "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-theme.conf)"
  sudo install -Dm644 "$checkout/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-wayland.conf" "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-wayland.conf)"
  sudo install -Dm644 "$checkout/default/sddm/hyprland.lua" "$(system_path /usr/share/sddm/hyprland.lua)"
  sudo install -Dm644 "$checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" "$(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop)"

  theme_source="$checkout/default/sddm/omarchy"
  theme_target=$(system_path /usr/share/sddm/themes/omarchy)
  sudo rm -rf -- "$theme_target"
  sudo install -d -m 0755 "$theme_target"
  while IFS= read -r -d '' theme_file; do
    relative_theme_file="${theme_file#"$theme_source"/}"
    sudo install -Dm644 "$theme_file" "$theme_target/$relative_theme_file"
  done < <(find "$theme_source" -type f -print0)

  login_config=$(mktemp)
  printf '[Users]\nRememberLastUser=true\nRememberLastSession=true\n' >"$login_config"
  sudo install -Dm644 "$login_config" "$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/99-omarchy-login.conf)"
  rm -f "$login_config"

  if [[ $operation == "setup" ]]; then
    # Setup explicitly requests authenticated login. Keep later host edits as
    # separate recovery copies without replacing the original rollback baseline.
    autologin_path=$(system_path /etc/sddm.conf.d/autologin.conf)
    if sudo test -e "$autologin_path" || sudo test -L "$autologin_path"; then
      transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id)
      preserved_dir=$(mktemp -d "$display_manager_state_root/transactions/$transaction_id/autologin-preserved.XXXXXXXX")
      sudo cp -aT "$autologin_path" "$preserved_dir/autologin.conf"
      echo "    removes: $autologin_path (recovery copy: $preserved_dir/autologin.conf)"
      sudo rm -f -- "$autologin_path"
    fi
    state_path=$(system_path /var/lib/sddm/state.conf)
    if ! sudo test -e "$state_path" && ! sudo test -L "$state_path"; then
      state_config=$(mktemp)
      printf '[Last]\nSession=omarchy.desktop\nUser=%s\n' "$current_user" >"$state_config"
      sudo install -Dm644 "$state_config" "$state_path"
      sudo chown sddm:sddm "$state_path"
      rm -f "$state_config"
    fi

    if [[ $(systemctl get-default) == "multi-user.target" ]]; then
      sudo systemctl set-default graphical.target
    fi
    sudo systemctl enable sddm.service
  fi
}

rollback_display_manager() {
  local transaction_id transaction_dir index path state previous_target

  transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id || true)
  if [[ -z $transaction_id ]] || ! validate_display_manager_transaction "$transaction_id"; then
    echo "Error: no valid active display-manager rollback record exists." >&2
    return 1
  fi
  transaction_dir="$display_manager_state_root/transactions/$transaction_id"

  echo "==> display-manager-rollback"
  echo "    restoring transaction: $transaction_id"
  for ((index = ${#display_manager_recorded_paths[@]} - 1; index >= 0; index--)); do
    path="${display_manager_recorded_paths[$index]}"
    state=$(<"$transaction_dir/path-$index-state")
    sudo rm -rf -- "$path"
    if [[ $state == "present" ]]; then
      sudo install -d -m 0755 "$(dirname "$path")"
      sudo cp -aT "$transaction_dir/backup/$index" "$path"
    fi
  done

  if [[ $(<"$transaction_dir/sddm-enabled-before") == "enabled" ]]; then
    if ! sudo systemctl enable sddm.service; then
      echo "Warning: could not restore SDDM's enabled state; continuing the file and target rollback." >&2
    fi
  else
    if ! sudo systemctl disable sddm.service; then
      echo "Warning: could not restore SDDM's disabled state; continuing the file and target rollback." >&2
    fi
  fi

  previous_target=$(<"$transaction_dir/default-target-before")
  if [[ $(systemctl get-default) != "$previous_target" ]]; then
    sudo systemctl set-default "$previous_target"
  fi

  printf '%s\n' "$(date --iso-8601=seconds)" >"$transaction_dir/rolled-back-at"
  rm -f "$display_manager_active_file"
  echo "    restored prior SDDM files and default target; attempted to restore the enabled state"
  echo "    retained packages: sddm qt6-wayland (safe, inert when the service is disabled)"
}

# The product uses the four-face basic package to keep fresh installs small.
# A plain Arch host may already carry the complete JetBrains Mono Nerd Font
# family, which is a functional superset but conflicts by package name. Keep
# that host choice instead of asking pacman to remove it during an overlay.
package_requirement_satisfied() {
  local package="$1"

  if pacman -Q "$package" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    return 0
  elif [[ $package == "ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd-basic" ]] && pacman -Q ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    return 0
  else
    return 1
  fi
}

# The path /etc/omarchy.conf resolves to, empty when unreadable. Existence is
# not enough: a conf pointing at another (or deleted) checkout would make the
# session load different code than the one being configured here.
linked_checkout() {
  [[ -f $omarchy_conf ]] || return 1
  (
    OMARCHY_PATH=""
    # shellcheck source=/dev/null
    . "$omarchy_conf" 2>/dev/null || true
    printf '%s' "${OMARCHY_PATH:-}"
  )
}

render_uwsm_environment() {
  cat <<'ENV'
# Written by omarchy-overlay-setup. uwsm doesn't source /etc/profile.d,
# so resolve OMARCHY_PATH, then load the packaged session environment
# (session defaults, user overrides, and optional tool activation) from the checkout.
[ -r /etc/omarchy.conf ] && . /etc/omarchy.conf
[ -r "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/bash/env-bootstrap" ] && . "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/bash/env-bootstrap"
[ -r "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy" ] && . "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy"
ENV
}

link_stage_complete() {
  local linked_path uwsm_env_file="$HOME/.config/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy"

  linked_path=$(linked_checkout || true)
  [[ -n $linked_path ]] || return 1
  [[ $(realpath -m "$linked_path" 2>/dev/null) == "$checkout" ]] || return 1
  [[ -f $uwsm_env_file ]] || return 1
  grep -Fqx '[ -r /etc/omarchy.conf ] && . /etc/omarchy.conf' "$uwsm_env_file" || return 1
  # These are the literal variable references the generated environment must contain.
  # shellcheck disable=SC2016
  grep -Fqx '[ -r "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/bash/env-bootstrap" ] && . "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/bash/env-bootstrap"' "$uwsm_env_file" || return 1
  # shellcheck disable=SC2016
  grep -Fqx '[ -r "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy" ] && . "${OMARCHY_PATH:-/usr/share/omarchy}/default/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy"' "$uwsm_env_file"
}

require_link() {
  local linked_path
  linked_path=$(linked_checkout || true)
  if [[ -z $linked_path ]]; then
    echo "Error: $omarchy_conf is missing — run 'omarchy overlay setup link' first." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if [[ $(realpath -m "$linked_path" 2>/dev/null) != "$checkout" ]]; then
    echo "Error: $omarchy_conf points at $linked_path, not this checkout — run 'omarchy overlay setup link' first." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
}

load_recorded_stages() {
  local output stage
  local -a stages=()

  recorded=()
  [[ -e $installation_conf ]] || return 1
  if ! output=$(
    OMARCHY_INSTALLATION_CONF_PATH="$installation_conf" \
      OMARCHY_RUNTIME_CONF_PATH="$omarchy_conf" \
      omarchy-overlay-stages
  ); then
    return 2
  fi
  mapfile -t stages <<<"$output"
  for stage in "${stages[@]}"; do
    recorded[$stage]=1
  done
}

write_recorded_stages() {
  local descriptor stage separator=""
  local stage_csv=""

  for stage in "${known_stages[@]}"; do
    if [[ -n ${recorded[$stage]:-} ]]; then
      stage_csv+="$separator$stage"
      separator=,
    fi
  done
  if [[ -z $stage_csv ]]; then
    echo "Error: refusing to write an empty desktop-overlay stage ledger." >&2
    return 1
  fi

  descriptor=$(mktemp)
  printf 'OMARCHY_INSTALLATION=desktop_overlay\nOMARCHY_DESKTOP_OWNER=%s\nOMARCHY_DESKTOP_STAGES=%s\n' \
    "$current_user" "$stage_csv" >"$descriptor"
  if ! sudo install -Dm644 "$descriptor" "$installation_conf"; then
    rm -f "$descriptor"
    return 1
  fi
  rm -f "$descriptor"
}

record_selected_stages() {
  local stage

  # The ledger was validated before mutation. Extend that in-memory baseline.
  for stage in "${known_stages[@]}"; do
    if stage_selected "$stage"; then
      recorded[$stage]=1
    fi
  done
  mark_overlay_migration_baseline
  write_recorded_stages
}

stage_recorded() {
  [[ -n ${recorded[$1]:-} ]]
}

require_recorded_selected_stages() {
  local stage

  if ! load_recorded_stages; then
    echo "Error: $installation_conf does not register a desktop overlay." >&2
    echo "Run 'omarchy overlay register <stage>...' before reconciliation." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
    if ! stage_recorded "$stage"; then
      echo "Error: package stage '$stage' is not recorded in $installation_conf." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  done
}

probe_registration_stage() {
  local stage="$1" package transaction_id
  local is_package_stage=0
  local -a stage_pkgs=()

  for package_stage in "${package_stages[@]}"; do
    if [[ $stage == "$package_stage" ]]; then
      is_package_stage=1
      mapfile -t stage_pkgs < <(group_packages "$stage")
      for package in "${stage_pkgs[@]}"; do
        if ! package_requirement_satisfied "$package"; then
          echo "Error: cannot register stage '$stage'; package '$package' is missing." >&2
          return 1
        fi
      done
      break
    fi
  done

  if (( is_package_stage )) && [[ $stage != "display-manager" ]]; then
    return 0
  fi

  case "$stage" in
    link)
      link_stage_complete || {
        echo "Error: cannot register stage 'link'; $omarchy_conf or the UWSM environment is missing or stale." >&2
        return 1
      }
      ;;
    config)
      config_stage_complete || {
        echo "Error: cannot register stage 'config'; its user configuration is incomplete." >&2
        return 1
      }
      ;;
    lock)
      [[ -f $(system_path /etc/pam.d/omarchy-lock-password) ]] || {
        echo "Error: cannot register stage 'lock'; its PAM service is absent." >&2
        return 1
      }
      ;;
    session-entry)
      cmp -s "$checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" \
        "$(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop)" || {
        echo "Error: cannot register stage 'session-entry'; its installed file does not match this checkout." >&2
        return 1
      }
      ;;
    display-manager)
      display_manager_configured || {
        echo "Error: cannot register stage 'display-manager'; SDDM is not fully configured." >&2
        return 1
      }
      transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id || true)
      if [[ -z $transaction_id ]] || ! validate_display_manager_transaction "$transaction_id"; then
        echo "Error: cannot register stage 'display-manager'; no valid pre-install rollback transaction exists." >&2
        echo "Register without display-manager, or restore the original transaction before adopting that stage." >&2
        return 1
      fi
      ;;
    core|audio|files|connectivity|capture|power)
      ;;
    *)
      echo "Error: cannot probe unknown desktop-overlay stage '$stage'." >&2
      return 1
      ;;
  esac
}

mark_overlay_migration_baseline() {
  local migration migration_dir="$checkout/migrations/desktop-overlay"
  local state_dir="${OMARCHY_OVERLAY_MIGRATION_STATE:-$HOME/.local/state/omarchy/desktop-overlay-migrations}"
  local baseline_marker="$state_dir/.baseline-established"

  mkdir -p "$state_dir"
  [[ ! -e $baseline_marker ]] || return 0
  for migration in "$migration_dir"/*.sh; do
    [[ -f $migration ]] || continue
    touch "$state_dir/${migration##*/}"
  done
  touch "$baseline_marker"
}

# Product status takes precedence over a stale overlay descriptor. Mutation
# still uses the ownership and product-package refusals below.
if stage_selected status; then
  echo "Omarchy desktop setup status (checkout: $checkout)"
  product_packages=()
  for product_pkg in omarchy omarchy-dev omarchy-settings omarchy-settings-dev; do
    if pacman -Q "$product_pkg" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      product_packages+=("$product_pkg")
    fi
  done
  if (( ${#product_packages[@]} > 0 )); then
    echo "  installation:  packaged Omarchy product"
    echo "  product:       ${product_packages[*]} installed"
    echo "  registration:  desktop overlay not applicable"
    exit 0
  fi
fi

# Repair corrects a ledger, it does not transfer the overlay or its per-user
# migration and rollback state. Rollback itself remains independent of a ledger.
if [[ -r $installation_conf ]] && ! stage_selected display-manager-rollback; then
  mapfile -t descriptor_types < <(sed -n -E 's/^[[:space:]]*OMARCHY_INSTALLATION=([^[:space:]#]+)[[:space:]]*(#.*)?$/\1/p' "$installation_conf")
  mapfile -t descriptor_owners < <(sed -n -E 's/^[[:space:]]*OMARCHY_DESKTOP_OWNER=([^[:space:]#]+)[[:space:]]*(#.*)?$/\1/p' "$installation_conf")
  if (( ${#descriptor_types[@]} == 1 && ${#descriptor_owners[@]} == 1 )) && [[ ${descriptor_types[0]} == "desktop_overlay" && ${descriptor_owners[0]} != "$current_user" ]]; then
    echo "Desktop overlay is registered to '${descriptor_owners[0]}'; run as that user." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# --- Read-only status report; never needs sudo and never writes.
if stage_selected status; then
  if [[ -e $installation_conf ]]; then
    if load_recorded_stages; then
      echo "  registration: desktop overlay owned by $current_user"
    else
      echo "  registration: invalid descriptor ($installation_conf)"
      echo "  repair: ./bin/omarchy-overlay-register --repair <stage>..."
      exit 1
    fi
  else
    echo "  registration: not registered"
  fi
  for stage in "${package_stages[@]}"; do
    mapfile -t stage_pkgs < <(group_packages "$stage")
    missing=0
    for package in "${stage_pkgs[@]}"; do
      package_requirement_satisfied "$package" || (( missing += 1 ))
    done
    if (( missing == 0 )); then
      state="complete (${#stage_pkgs[@]} packages)"
    else
      state="$missing of ${#stage_pkgs[@]} packages missing"
    fi
    if stage_recorded "$stage"; then
      echo "  $stage: $state; recorded"
    else
      echo "  $stage: $state; not recorded"
    fi
  done
  linked_path=$(linked_checkout || true)
  if [[ -z $linked_path ]]; then
    state="not linked ($omarchy_conf absent)"
  elif [[ $(realpath -m "$linked_path" 2>/dev/null) == "$checkout" ]]; then
    state="linked to this checkout"
  else
    state="points at $linked_path, not this checkout"
  fi
  if stage_recorded link; then
    state+="; recorded"
  else
    state+="; not recorded"
  fi
  echo "  link: $state"
  if [[ -f $HOME/.config/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy ]]; then
    echo "  link: uwsm environment present"
  else
    echo "  link: uwsm environment absent"
  fi
  if config_stage_complete; then
    state="seeded (theme: $(cat "$HOME/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme.name" 2>/dev/null || echo none))"
  else
    state="not seeded"
  fi
  if stage_recorded config; then
    state+="; recorded"
  else
    state+="; not recorded"
  fi
  echo "  config: $state"
  if [[ -f $(system_path /etc/pam.d/omarchy-lock-password) ]]; then
    state="PAM services present"
  else
    state="PAM services absent"
  fi
  if stage_recorded lock; then
    state+="; recorded"
  else
    state+="; not recorded"
  fi
  echo "  lock: $state"
  if [[ -f $(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop) ]]; then
    state="present"
  else
    state="absent"
  fi
  if stage_recorded session-entry; then
    state+="; recorded"
  else
    state+="; not recorded"
  fi
  echo "  session-entry: $state"
  if display_manager_configured; then
    state="configured and enabled"
  else
    state="not configured"
  fi
  if stage_recorded display-manager; then
    state+="; recorded"
  else
    state+="; not recorded"
  fi
  echo "  display-manager: $state"
  if transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id 2>/dev/null) && validate_display_manager_transaction "$transaction_id"; then
    echo "  display-manager-rollback: available (transaction $transaction_id)"
  elif [[ -f $display_manager_active_file ]]; then
    echo "  display-manager-rollback: invalid active record"
  else
    echo "  display-manager-rollback: unavailable"
  fi
  if (( status_only )); then
    exit 0
  fi
fi

# --- Everything below acts on the system.

if stage_selected config; then
  # The same normalization and validation omarchy-theme-set applies, so every
  # bad value fails here, before sudo and before the system has been modified.
  raw_theme=$theme
  theme=$(echo "$theme" | sed -E 's/<[^>]+>//g' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | tr ' ' '-')
  if [[ -z $theme || $theme == .* || $theme == */* ]]; then
    echo "Error: invalid theme name: $raw_theme" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if [[ ! -d $checkout/themes/$theme ]]; then
    echo "Error: theme '$theme' does not exist under $checkout/themes" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  for branding_source in "$checkout/icon.txt" "$checkout/logo.txt"; do
    if [[ ! -f $branding_source ]]; then
      echo "Error: required branding source is missing: $branding_source" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  done
  for branding_target in "$HOME/.config/omarchy/branding/about.txt" "$HOME/.config/omarchy/branding/screensaver.txt"; do
    if [[ -L $branding_target && ! -e $branding_target ]]; then
      echo "Error: refusing to replace dangling branding symlink: $branding_target" >&2
      exit 1
    elif [[ -e $branding_target && ! -f $branding_target ]]; then
      echo "Error: refusing to replace non-file branding path: $branding_target" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  done
fi

# This bootstrap is for systems the Omarchy product did not install. On a
# packaged install the desktop is already set up; pointing it at a checkout
# is omarchy-dev-link's job.
for product_pkg in omarchy omarchy-dev omarchy-settings omarchy-settings-dev; do
  if pacman -Q "$product_pkg" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Error: the $product_pkg package is installed — this system was set up by the Omarchy product." >&2
    echo "Use omarchy-dev-link to point an Omarchy install at a checkout instead." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
done

if [[ $operation == "setup" && ! -e $installation_conf ]] && stage_selected core && ! stage_selected link; then
  existing_checkout=$(linked_checkout || true)
  if [[ -n $existing_checkout && $(realpath -m "$existing_checkout" 2>/dev/null) == "$checkout" ]]; then
    echo "Error: this checkout is already linked as an unregistered desktop overlay." >&2
    echo "Adopt the existing installation in one step before adding or reapplying stages:" >&2
    echo "  ./bin/omarchy-overlay-register core link config audio files connectivity capture power lock session-entry display-manager" >&2
    echo "Omit stages that are not installed. If this is an incomplete new setup, run 'omarchy overlay setup core link' instead." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

if (( setup_core_repair )); then
  if [[ ! -e $installation_conf ]]; then
    echo "Error: setup core --repair needs an existing invalid descriptor; use setup core for a new overlay." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if load_recorded_stages >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Error: $installation_conf already contains a valid overlay ledger; run setup core without --repair." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

if [[ -e $installation_conf ]] && ! { [[ $operation == "register" ]] && (( repair_registration )); } && (( ! setup_core_repair )) && ! stage_selected display-manager-rollback; then
  if ! load_recorded_stages; then
    echo "Repair it with 'omarchy overlay register --repair <stage>...' after verifying the installed stages." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# Status must remain able to diagnose a stale link, and selecting link is the
# repair. Every other operation against an already-linked overlay must run from
# the checkout /etc/omarchy.conf names; otherwise it could reconcile one tree
# while the next desktop session executes another.
if [[ -e $installation_conf && -n ${recorded[link]:-} && -z ${selected[status]:-} && -z ${selected[display-manager-rollback]:-} && -z ${selected[link]:-} ]]; then
  require_link
fi

if [[ $operation == "packages" || $operation == "artifacts" ]]; then
  require_recorded_selected_stages
fi

if [[ $operation == "setup" && -z ${selected[status]:-} && -z ${selected[display-manager-rollback]:-} ]]; then
  if [[ ! -e $installation_conf && -z ${selected[core]:-} ]]; then
    echo "Error: begin a new overlay with 'omarchy overlay setup core', or register an existing overlay with 'omarchy overlay register <stage>...'." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
    if [[ $stage != "core" ]] && ! stage_selected core && ! stage_recorded core; then
      echo "Error: setup stage '$stage' requires the core stage to be recorded first." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if [[ $stage == "config" || $stage == "display-manager" ]] && ! stage_selected link && ! stage_recorded link; then
      echo "Error: setup stage '$stage' requires the link stage to be recorded first." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if [[ $stage == "display-manager" ]] && ! stage_selected config && ! stage_recorded config; then
      echo "Error: setup stage 'display-manager' requires the config stage to be recorded first." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  done
fi

if [[ $operation == "register" ]]; then
  if [[ -e $installation_conf ]] && (( ! repair_registration )); then
    echo "Error: $installation_conf already exists; use setup stages to extend a registered overlay, or register --repair to replace a stale descriptor." >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
    if [[ $stage != "core" ]] && ! stage_selected core; then
      echo "Error: registering '$stage' also requires the core stage to be recorded." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if [[ $stage == "config" || $stage == "display-manager" ]] && ! stage_selected link; then
      echo "Error: registering '$stage' also requires the link stage to be recorded." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if [[ $stage == "display-manager" ]] && ! stage_selected config; then
      echo "Error: registering 'display-manager' also requires the config stage to be recorded." >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  done

  for stage in "${known_stages[@]}"; do
    if stage_selected "$stage"; then
      echo "==> verify $stage"
      probe_registration_stage "$stage"
      recorded[$stage]=1
    fi
  done

  sudo -v
  mark_overlay_migration_baseline
  write_recorded_stages
  if (( repair_registration )); then
    echo "Repaired desktop-overlay registration in $installation_conf"
  else
    echo "Registered desktop overlay in $installation_conf"
  fi
  exit 0
fi

if stage_selected display-manager-rollback; then
  transaction_id=$(display_manager_transaction_id || true)
  if [[ -z $transaction_id ]] || ! validate_display_manager_transaction "$transaction_id"; then
    echo "Error: no valid active display-manager rollback record exists." >&2
    echo "Nothing can be restored; repair the registration with the currently installed stages while omitting display-manager." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  sudo -v
  rollback_display_manager
  if [[ -e $installation_conf ]]; then
    if load_recorded_stages; then
      unset 'recorded[display-manager]'
      if ! cmp -s "$checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" \
        "$(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop)"; then
        unset 'recorded[session-entry]'
      fi
      write_recorded_stages
    else
      echo "Warning: the invalid installation descriptor was left unchanged; repair it separately with 'omarchy overlay register --repair <stage>...'." >&2
    fi
  fi
  exit 0
fi

# Validate the staged dependency graph before a package transaction or any
# other write. In particular, "core config" without link must not upgrade the
# system and only then discover that config cannot run.
if stage_selected config && ! stage_selected link; then
  require_link
fi

if stage_selected display-manager && [[ $operation != "packages" && $operation != "register" ]]; then
  if ! stage_selected link; then
    require_link
  fi
  if [[ $operation == "setup" ]] && ! stage_selected config && ! config_stage_complete; then
    echo "Error: display-manager needs the seeded desktop config — run 'omarchy overlay setup config' first." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  preflight_display_manager
fi

if [[ $operation == "artifacts" ]]; then
  if stage_selected lock && [[ ! -x $checkout/bin/omarchy-apply-lock ]]; then
    echo "Error: lock artifact source is missing: $checkout/bin/omarchy-apply-lock" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if stage_selected session-entry && [[ ! -f $checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop ]]; then
    echo "Error: session-entry artifact source is missing: $checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# Update-time preflight intentionally runs before package reconciliation. It
# validates checkout sources and rollback integrity, but does not require the
# packages that the next step is responsible for restoring.
if (( check_artifacts )); then
  exit 0
fi

requires_core=0
for stage in "${!selected[@]}"; do
  if [[ $stage != "core" && $stage != "status" && $stage != "display-manager-rollback" ]]; then
    requires_core=1
    break
  fi
done
if (( requires_core )) && ! stage_selected core; then
  mapfile -t core_pkgs < <(group_packages core)
  missing_core_pkgs=()
  for package in "${core_pkgs[@]}"; do
    package_requirement_satisfied "$package" || missing_core_pkgs+=("$package")
  done
  if (( ${#missing_core_pkgs[@]} > 0 )); then
    echo "Error: the core stage is incomplete — run 'omarchy overlay setup core' first." >&2
    echo "Missing core packages: ${missing_core_pkgs[*]}" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# --- Packages for every selected package stage, in one transaction.
packages=()
if [[ $operation != "artifacts" ]]; then
  for stage in "${package_stages[@]}"; do
    if stage_selected "$stage"; then
      mapfile -t stage_pkgs < <(group_packages "$stage")
      echo "==> $stage"
      echo "    packages: ${stage_pkgs[*]}"
      for package in "${stage_pkgs[@]}"; do
        if [[ $package == "ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd-basic" ]] && pacman -Q ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd >/dev/null 2>&1; then
          echo "    preserving installed package: ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd (satisfies $package)"
        else
          packages+=("$package")
        fi
      done
    fi
  done
fi

if (( ${#packages[@]} > 0 )) || { [[ $operation == "setup" ]] && (( ! status_only )); }; then
  # A full upgrade on a fresh Arch system can outlive sudo's timestamp. Keep
  # the credential alive so later selected stages do not fail halfway through
  # the setup or prompt again after the package transaction.
  # shellcheck source=/dev/null
  source "$checkout/bin/omarchy-sudo-keepalive"
elif (( ! status_only )); then
  sudo -v
fi

if [[ $operation == "setup" || $operation == "packages" ]] && stage_selected core; then
  ensure_overlay_package_source
fi

if (( ${#packages[@]} > 0 )); then
  echo "Installing selected package stages (full system upgrade)"
  pacman_args=(-Syu --needed)
  if [[ $operation == "packages" || ${OMARCHY_UPDATE_UNATTENDED:-0} == "1" ]]; then
    pacman_args+=(--noconfirm)
  fi
  sudo pacman "${pacman_args[@]}" "${packages[@]}"
fi

if [[ $operation == "packages" ]]; then
  exit 0
fi

# --- link: point the system and the uwsm session at this checkout.
if stage_selected link; then
  echo "==> link"
  echo "    writes: $omarchy_conf (the dev sudoers policy is NOT installed)"
  echo "    writes: ~/.config/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy (existing file backed up to ~/.config/uwsm/backups/)"
  omarchy_write_runtime_link "$checkout" 0 "$omarchy_conf" "$(system_path /etc/sudoers.d/omarchy-dev-path)"

  install -d "$HOME/.config/uwsm/env.d"
  uwsm_env_file="$HOME/.config/uwsm/env.d/10-omarchy"
  uwsm_env_staged=$(mktemp)
  # Static content on purpose: the checkout path lives only in /etc/omarchy.conf,
  # where the shared runtime-link writer already wrote it correctly quoted, so no pathname
  # needs escaping here and the file keeps working if the checkout is re-linked.
  render_uwsm_environment >"$uwsm_env_staged"
  if [[ -f $uwsm_env_file ]] && ! cmp -s "$uwsm_env_staged" "$uwsm_env_file"; then
    # uwsm sources every file in env.d, so a backup left in that directory
    # would be executed right after the file that replaced it. Keep backups
    # outside the sourced directory.
    uwsm_backup_dir="$HOME/.config/uwsm/backups"
    uwsm_env_backup="$uwsm_backup_dir/10-omarchy.bak.$(date +%s)"
    install -d "$uwsm_backup_dir"
    cp -f "$uwsm_env_file" "$uwsm_env_backup"
    echo "Backed up existing $uwsm_env_file to $uwsm_env_backup"
  fi
  install -m 0644 "$uwsm_env_staged" "$uwsm_env_file"
  rm -f "$uwsm_env_staged"
fi

# --- config: user-level desktop configuration. Requires link, because the
# seeded configs and the session resolve everything through /etc/omarchy.conf.
if stage_selected config; then
  echo "==> config"
  require_link
  echo "    writes: ~/.local/share/fonts/omarchy.ttf, ~/.config desktop configs (backups kept),"
  echo "    writes: missing ~/.config/omarchy/branding/{about,screensaver}.txt defaults (existing files preserved),"
  echo "    writes: theme state under ~/.local/state/omarchy/, btop theme link, first-run marker"

  install -Dm644 "$checkout/default/fonts/omarchy/omarchy.ttf" "$HOME/.local/share/fonts/omarchy.ttf"
  fc-cache -f >/dev/null

  branding_dir="$HOME/.config/omarchy/branding"
  install -d "$branding_dir"
  if [[ ! -e $branding_dir/about.txt ]]; then
    install -m 0644 "$checkout/icon.txt" "$branding_dir/about.txt"
  fi
  if [[ ! -e $branding_dir/screensaver.txt ]]; then
    install -m 0644 "$checkout/logo.txt" "$branding_dir/screensaver.txt"
  fi

  if (( all_configs )); then
    echo "Seeding every shipped config from $checkout/config (existing files are backed up)"
    seed_roots=("$checkout/config")
  else
    echo "Seeding desktop configs from $checkout/config (existing files are backed up)"
    seed_roots=()
    for config_dir in "${desktop_configs[@]}"; do
      if [[ -e $checkout/config/$config_dir ]]; then
        seed_roots+=("$checkout/config/$config_dir")
      fi
    done
  fi
  while IFS= read -r -d '' config_file; do
    omarchy-refresh-config "${config_file#"$checkout"/config/}"
  done < <(find "${seed_roots[@]}" -type f -print0)

  echo "Generating the initial theme: $theme"
  OMARCHY_THEME_HEADLESS=1 omarchy-theme-set "$theme"

  # Headless generation avoids restarting applications while the checkout is
  # being seeded, but it also skips the GNOME/GTK synchronization that normal
  # first-run provisioning performs. Apply that narrow user-session hook so
  # GTK and libadwaita applications match the selected light/dark mode and use
  # the product's icon theme before first-run is marked complete below.
  omarchy-theme-set-gnome

  mkdir -p "$HOME/.config/btop/themes"
  ln -snf "$HOME/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/btop.theme" "$HOME/.config/btop/themes/current.theme"

  # The default session autostart runs omarchy-provision-first-run, which
  # enables user units and finalization the packaged product ships. None of
  # that exists on a checkout-only install; mark it complete so first login
  # doesn't try.
  omarchy-done mark first-run-user

  cat <<DONE

Desktop configured from: $checkout

Test the session from a TTY with:
  uwsm start -g -1 -e -D Hyprland hyprland.desktop
DONE
fi

# --- files: register the default directory handler once the file manager exists.
if stage_selected files; then
  if omarchy-cmd-present xdg-mime; then
    echo "==> files: registering nautilus as the inode/directory handler"
    xdg-mime default org.gnome.Nautilus.desktop inode/directory
  else
    echo "==> files: xdg-mime not available; skip registering the default directory handler" >&2
  fi
fi

# --- lock: explicit opt-in PAM services for the shell's lock screen.
if stage_selected lock; then
  echo "==> lock"
  echo "    writes: /etc/pam.d/omarchy-lock-* (new PAM services; nothing existing is modified)"
  omarchy-apply-lock
fi

# A display-manager run owns the session entry as part of its rollback boundary,
# so capture the baseline immediately before either stage writes that file.
if stage_selected display-manager; then
  echo "==> display-manager"
  echo "    rollback: records the prior SDDM files, enabled state, and default target before configuration"
  begin_display_manager_transaction
fi

# --- session-entry: explicit opt-in greeter session file.
if stage_selected session-entry; then
  echo "==> session-entry"
  echo "    writes: /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop"
  sudo install -Dm644 "$checkout/default/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop" "$(system_path /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions/omarchy.desktop)"
fi

# --- display-manager: explicit SDDM integration. It runs after the independent
# session entry, using the baseline recorded immediately before that entry was
# written. The service is enabled, never started in-place.
if stage_selected display-manager; then
  apply_display_manager
fi

if [[ $operation == "artifacts" ]]; then
  exit 0
fi

if (( setup_core_repair )); then
  descriptor_backup="$installation_conf.omarchy-overlay-repair.$(date +%s%N).bak"
  probe_registration_stage core
  recorded=()
  recorded[core]=1
  mark_overlay_migration_baseline
  sudo mv -- "$installation_conf" "$descriptor_backup"
  if ! write_recorded_stages; then
    sudo mv -- "$descriptor_backup" "$installation_conf"
    echo "Error: could not write the repaired overlay descriptor; restored the original from $descriptor_backup." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  echo "Repaired desktop-overlay registration in $installation_conf"
  echo "Previous descriptor: $descriptor_backup"
  exit 0
fi

record_selected_stages

cat <<'DONE'

Left unconfigured, deliberately: bootloader, initramfs, Secure Boot,
encryption, storage, Snapper, general system services, and the
omarchy/omarchy-settings packages. SDDM is configured and enabled only when
the explicit display-manager stage is selected. The optional user units a
packaged install enables (bluetooth pairing agent, sleep lock, ...) were not
set up either; see install/user/first-run/enable-user-units.sh for that list.
Run "omarchy overlay status" to see what is and isn't in place.
DONE
